    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Once upon a time, there was a man who had four sons. One day, he told each of his sons to go and see what a pear tree looked like during winter, spring, summer and autumn. After a year, he "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "gathered",
            "ref": "v-gather"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " them together to ask them what they had seen."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The first son answered that the tree had been "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bare",
            "ref": "v-bare"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and ugly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The second son said, “No! It "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "was covered with",
            "ref": "v-be-covered-with"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " new green leaves. The tree had bright hopes.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The third son shook his head. He said the pear tree had "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "been full of",
            "ref": "v-be-full-of"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " flowers. They smelled so sweet and looked so beautiful."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“There were many pears on the tree, but no flowers,” the fourth son "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "disagreed",
            "ref": "v-disagree"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “I saw the joy of a good "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "harvest",
            "ref": "v-harvest"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ".”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The man then said to his sons that they were all right. They got different answers because each of them had seen only one season in the life of the pear tree."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“You cannot judge a tree, a person or your life by just one season. If you give up in the winter, you will miss the hope of your spring, the beauty of your summer and the harvest of your autumn.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
